          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Check if replacing subtraction by addition in this way does not change the value of the expression, by taking different examples.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.174,
            0.556,
            0.212
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Let us take the numbers. 18 and 10 18 – 10 = 8 and 18 + (– 10) = 8"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.231,
            0.883,
            0.289
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you explain why subtracting a number is the same as adding its inverse, using the Token Model of integers that we saw in the Class 6 textbook of mathematics?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.304,
            0.698,
            0.323
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Refer chapter 10 of class VI Mathematics Textbook."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.337,
            0.882,
            0.416
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Does changing the order in which the terms are added give different values? Ans:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " No, For example, 14 + 10 +( – 5) = 19 or (– 5) + 10 + 14 = 19"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.425,
            0.24,
            0.444
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Page No. 29"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
